      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Subject: Ensuring Ergonomic Excellence in Your Remote Workstations\n\nDear Team,\n\nAs we continue to navigate the ever-evolving landscape of remote work, it's crucial to maintain a harmonious balance between productivity and well-being. To that end, we want to remind you of the importance of setting up your workstations ergonomically. Proper desk setup is essential to prevent wrist and back pain, ensuring that you can work comfortably and efficiently.\n\nConsider your desk as a fortress, where your body is the king. Just as a king needs a throne that supports his every move, your body needs a workspace that supports your health. Here are some ergonomic tips to help you fortify your fortress:\n\n1. **Chair and Desk Alignment**: Your chair should be adjustable, allowing you to sit with your feet flat on the ground and your knees at a 90-degree angle. Your desk should be at a height where your elbows are at a 90-degree angle when typing.\n\n2. **Monitor Placement**: Position your monitor at eye level, about an arm's length away. This will help reduce strain on your neck and eyes, much like how a watchful guard keeps an eye on the castle walls.\n\n3. **Keyboard and Mouse Position**: Keep your keyboard",
      "source": "target",
